    "body": "## Summary\n- restrict expense claim evidence to PDF, JPEG, PNG and WebP attachments\n- reject unsupported media before mutating expense escrow or creating a claim\n- add regression coverage proving arbitrary participant attachments cannot enter the reimbursement audit trail\n\n## Why\nExpense claims feed directly into fee-free reimbursement at completion. A generic private attachment should not automatically qualify as financial receipt evidence. Constraining claims to reviewable receipt/document formats makes the audit trail safer and easier to moderate while preserving the existing participant-only attachment privacy model.\n\n## Migration\nNo Flyway migration is required.\n\n## Validation\nDo not merge until all latest-head required CI/checks complete successfully.",
